- Move fire and forget things to be processed on Worker
- Adjust on Email message generation with EmailMessage Facotry
- Use Mediator instead Mediatr for free performance gains, see [https://github.com/martinothamar/Mediator#2-benchmarks](https://github.com/martinothamar/Mediator#2-benchmarks)
- Adjust naming
   - Commands execute state changes;
   - Queries only read data;
   - Events are processed in-process;
   - Messages are processed out of process by the Worker;
   - Worker has MessageDispatchers that invokes the MessageHandlers from the Application (like the WebAPI with controllers calling command and queries);

 This PR adds support for iterable arguments  for query with `IN`-operators for `RealmResults`, `RealmList` and `RealmSet`
  ```dart
    final listOfNames = ['Ani', 'Teddy'];
    var result = realm.query<Person>(r'name IN $0', [listOfNames]);

    final setOfNames = {'Poly', 'Teddy'};
    result = realm.query<Person>(r'name IN $0', [setOfNames]);

    final iterableNames = result.map((e) => e.name);
    result = realm.query<Person>(r'name IN $0', [iterableNames]);
  ```
Added support for query on `RealmSet`.
Allow list of nullable objects when querying on `RealmList` and `RealmSet`. It was supported only for `RealmResults` before.
Fixes #755
Fixes #1084
